invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_post.h
catches: unit
reason: hspost_ticket_age_ok starts from a cap of about 49.7 days rather
  than seven, so a config that gives no lifetime, and one that gives the
  lifetime above seven days a server must not send, offer a ticket up to
  seven weeks old. RFC 9846 section
  4.6.1 forbids a client a ticket older than seven days whatever its
  lifetime says. The rows for a lifetime of 0 and of 604801 seconds
  require the first millisecond past seven days to be refused.

--- old
    uint32_t lifetime_s = CH_TICKET_LIFETIME_MAX;
--- new
    uint32_t lifetime_s = UINT32_MAX / 1000U;
